  <prompt>
    Execute Track-B batch 2 of FR-TB-01: delete the SpaarkeAi-page Insights renderer cluster (~14 files + tests — R5-origin from PR #345, never wired, superseded by R6 Pillar 5, claimed by no active project per `notes/agent-findings-engine-projects.md`) plus the rest of the SpaarkeAi-page deadwood from inventory §9. This batch rides alongside wave W-P0-B; the files are dead by definition, so there is no overlap with live-code tasks. Per NFR-08, every deletion is grep-zero-verified with SHOWN output and builds proven green; evidence lands in `notes/track-b/batch-2-evidence.md`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Frontend developer (React/TypeScript) experienced with the SpaarkeAi code-page structure (`src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/**`) — precise at removing dead components and their vestigial import/reference sites without disturbing live panes.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Every batch-2 item below is deleted (or recorded keep-with-reason if found live), grep-zero shown per deleted symbol, `npm run build:prod` for SpaarkeAi green with shown output, TASK-INDEX updated, and `notes/track-b/batch-2-evidence.md` written.
  </goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="design-spec">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-plan">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/plan.md</file>
