      <item>Task 045 (FR-P3-06) decomposes ConversationPane — this batch only strips dead references from it</item>
    </related-work>
  </context>

  <steps>
    <step order="0" name="Context check">
      Check context usage. If &gt; 70%, create handoff summary and request new chat. Load inputs; read inventory §9 (SpaarkeAi page) and the migration map Track-B list; read notes/agent-findings-engine-projects.md for the renderer-cluster liveness verdict.
    </step>
    <step order="1" name="Read and confirm the batch list">
      Enumerate the Insights renderer cluster files (~14 + tests) and the other four item groups via Glob/Grep; capture exact paths. Confirm zero importers for each. Any item with a live importer outside the batch → keep-with-reason.
    </step>
    <step order="2" name="Delete the batch">
      Delete confirmed-dead files and tests; strip the vestigial references from WorkspacePane/ConversationPane (imports, dead props/branches referencing deleted components only).
    </step>
    <step order="3" name="Grep-zero verification (SHOWN)">
      For each deleted component/symbol (each renderer-cluster component name, `notificationContextLoader`, `SendToWorkspaceButton`, `PinToMatterButton`, `AddToAssistantToggle`, `ChatHistoryPanel`): grep across src/ and SHOW the zero-hit output. Note the SpaarkeAi-wrapper vs any same-name shared-lib component distinction explicitly if applicable.
    </step>
    <step order="4" name="Build verification (SHOWN)">
      Run `npm run build:prod` for the SpaarkeAi solution (and any touched shared package); show green output. Run touched-surface tests.
    </step>
    <step order="5" name="Evidence + close">
      Write `projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/track-b/batch-2-evidence.md` (item table: deleted-path / grep output / keep-with-reason). Update TASK-INDEX.md (071 → ✅). Report completion.
    </step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">build:prod + tests for SpaarkeAi</tool>
    <tool name="git">Version control (deletions preserved in history)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
